  "prompt": "What penalties apply to late filing of a VAT return?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nPenalties for late filing of a VAT return include a fine of 25% of the tax due, plus interest at the rate of 12% per annum on the unpaid tax from the due date until the date of payment.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, businesses must ensure that their VAT returns are filed on or before the due date to avoid incurring significant penalties. The combination of a substantial surcharge and accruing interest can lead to increased tax liabilities, impacting cash flow and financial planning. Timely filing not only avoids these penalties but also fosters good standing with the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR).",
